## Q21 (gui-stack-v1-issues) — a generic struct/class whose type parameter is
## "phantom" (not determined by any constructor argument) must still infer its
## generic args from the call's expected type. Before the fix `Sig.new(id)`
## produced the bare head `Sig` (no generic args) and failed to unify with the
## declared return `Sig[T]`. Now un-inferable params become fresh inference
## vars that the surrounding context binds.

struct Sig[T]
  id: Int
end

def make[T](id: Int) -> Sig[T]
  Sig.new(id)
end

def main
  let s: Sig[Int] = make(7)
  puts "id=#{s.id}"
  let t: Sig[String] = make(99)
  puts "id=#{t.id}"
end
